#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114946 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eaea1ecf-d6b9-5807-8776-17359e94336b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Definite Integral Using the Constant Multiple Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "4036785f-d99b-5c01-81e9-edfb93cc1f0d" :question/math-academy-id "e-413" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{2}9x^{2}dx &= 9\\int_{-1}^{2}x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.3x^{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) \\\\\n&= 3(8 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 9 \\\\\n&= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f236feb9-761b-544b-b34a-19eb46c28988" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Integral of the Sum of Two Functions Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "6ecec0d3-1714-550b-bce2-88ead5abf2f4" :question/math-academy-id "e-414" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/4} (\\sec x \\tan x - \\cos x)\\, \\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/4}(\\sec x\\tan x - \\cos x)dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\sec x\\tan xdx - \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\cos xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\sec x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} - \\left.\\sin x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} \\\\\n&= (\\sec \\frac{π}{4} - \\sec 0) - (\\sin \\frac{π}{4} - \\sin 0) \\\\\n&= (\\sqrt{2} - 1) - (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114958 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cff6bd5-aeb6-55ed-a44b-fca322e73dd8" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Integral of a Polynomial Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d5d4992c-4c68-5d30-b7b7-a5a89e4cc3e4" :question/math-academy-id "e-415" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^2(2x^3 - 5)\\, \\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{2}(2x^{3} - 5)dx &= 2\\int_{-2}^{2}x^{3}dx - 5\\int_{-2}^{2}1dx \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{2}x^{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(2^{4} - (-2)^{4}) - 5(2 - (-2)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(16 - 16) - 5 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&=-20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114964 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c5a147-0100-5f4b-a221-25b8674b2115" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Integral of a Sum of Two Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "0347b53a-4f7c-587e-9232-aa9be2065576" :question/math-academy-id "e-416" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_1^4 \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_1^4 \\left(x^{1/2}-2x^{-2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{2}{x^{2}})dx &= \\int_{1}^{4}x^{1/2}dx - 2\\int_{1}^{4}x^{-2}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}\\right|_{1}^{4} + \\left.2x^{-1}\\right|_{1}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(4^{3/2} - 1^{3/2}) + 2(4^{-1} - 1^{-1}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(8 - 1) + 2(\\frac{1}{4} - 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} + 2 \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{19}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c5a147-0100-5f4b-a221-25b8674b2115" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Integral of a Sum of Two Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86e151a9-ebb0-50d6-94b7-e00972d1639d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113229} {:answer/id #uuid "8d59dc5f-ea34-5a53-8373-8652c81a9e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113230} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d7f713-2771-5d07-9f96-7a990493c7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113231} {:answer/id #uuid "379cc5db-7ce4-5419-ae0b-cf69dd935dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113232} {:answer/id #uuid "66696cb0-7005-505e-a066-dd3ea7d9f23b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66696cb0-7005-505e-a066-dd3ea7d9f23b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{211}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113233} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7d658c8-af0f-5950-986b-bfb1c8afa44d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113228}] :question/id #uuid "00be2488-9ecc-5429-aabc-0015493fbd7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-29784" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}} + \\frac{x}{10})dx$?"}]}
